filex-office-editor (scripts/x2t): CryptPad's changes to ONLYOFFICE core
for WebAssembly, ported to ONLYOFFICE core v9.4.0.129 by BRF Tech on
2026-10-10.

From https://github.com/cryptpad/onlyoffice-x2t-wasm (AGPL-3.0-or-later):
its core/ at tag v9.3.0+0 compared with ONLYOFFICE core v9.3.0.140 (the
commit that tag's core/ was pulled from), applied to v9.4.0.129 three-way.

Kept, as CryptPad has them:
  - the build files of the libraries x2t links: no ICU of core's own
    (emscripten's), no second copy of zlib or of minizip's two programs,
    no UnicodeConverter, kernel or CryptoPP linked into a library that
    another one links again, the text shaper kept on (core turns it off
    for a gcc older than 5, and em++ answers -dumpversion with its own
    4.0.11), three sources DocxFormatLib needs, Qt left out of the CSS
    calculator;
  - doctrenderer without a JavaScript engine: CryptPad's doctrenderer,
    docbuilder and docbuilder_p stand-ins (*_empty.cpp, put in place of
    the three by steps.sh), the engine's sources out of doctrenderer.pri
    and js_base.pri, one include path;
  - HtmlFile2's replace_all and EncodeXmlString renamed (they clashed with
    functions of the same name elsewhere at the link);
  - the FB2 converter left out of x2t (Fb2File is not built);
  - x2t's memory limit (proclimits) left out;
  - pdf.bin read from beside the document, where the page puts it.

Left out, because 9.4 does not need them or they do not apply there:
Common/base.pri (CryptPad's tree carries an older copy of the whole file;
02-wasm-link-flags.patch makes the two changes the link needs),
MsBinaryFile's CBinaryReader moved into its header (9.4's declaration and
definition agree), boost_regex unlinked in boost.pri (steps.sh builds it),
a blank line in CCssCalculator_Private.cpp, a list of headers in
OdfFormatLib.pro, a test file renamed.

git apply reads from the first "diff --git" line on.

